  "provenance": {
    "label": "synthetic deployment-matrix mission diagnostic (features_only privacy)",
    "assets": "OpenAI-generated synthetic humans (owner-supplied); NOT real people, NOT real aerial data",
    "note": "local/head latency and energy are bench measurements of inference on a devkit (no flight load, no radio, lab thermals); results are still mission-simulation diagnostics, never real-UAV performance",
    "design": "model catalog: model_family x execution_mode, policy selects one config_id. Family deeplabv3_resnet50: onboard fp32, onboard fp16 (reduced precision via the torch kind's dtype knob; int8 needs TensorRT and stays out of scope), raw-RGB full offload (deliberately privacy-forbidden under this features_only contract), and TWO predefined-split tiers (pretrained_split kind): Entropic Student DeepLabV3-R50 beta 0.64 / 5.12 from the SC2 benchmark -- the split point is the SOURCE PAPER'S, adopted as a fixed catalog option, never searched or tuned here (provenance embedded per config). Family lraspp_mobilenet_v3_large: onboard fp32 / fp16 only -- no published split configuration for this architecture was found, and inventing one is forbidden, so the family honestly lacks a split tier. Wire payloads for pretrained_split are priced from the entropy-coded bitstream the head actually produces per frame (communication_mb_per_call is the nominal documentation value, measured on this world's frames at 512x384 input on CPU); head_latency_s, energy_j_per_call (head), and remote_compute_s are CONFIGURED mission-scale placeholders PENDING board measurement (the sc2 encoder is ~0.14M params). The checkpoints are local-only (gitignored cache), like the model-zoo weights. VOC-trained checkpoints on synthetic aerial markers are a documented domain mismatch (as in V2.1): this scenario exercises the catalog/accounting/privacy semantics, not attainable perception quality. EXTENDED 2026-08-11: three more catalog rows. presplit_ghnd_bq3 = the SC2 release's second published method family (GHND bottleneck + 8-bit quantization, no entropy coding; measured 39.6 KB on this world's frames -- vs 12.6 KB entropic-coded, the honest cost of skipping the entropy coder). maskrcnn_onboard_full + presplit_maskrcnn_fcm = a second MODEL FAMILY (instance segmentation, torchvision official COCO weights): full onboard, and split at the MPEG FCM standard FPN test point (uint8-reduced features measured 4.19 MB -- the standard's learned feature codec is out of scope, and the resulting payload gap vs trained bottlenecks is a finding). A float32 FCM split reproduces the onboard model's mask exactly (pinned by the opt-in real-model test). Mask R-CNN costs are configured mission-scale placeholders pending board measurement, like the other rows. HARDWARE-GROUNDED VARIANT (MODE_30W_ALL): onboard mission_latency_s / energy_j_per_call and split-head head_latency_s / energy_j_per_call are MEASURED ABSOLUTE values (Jetson AGX Xavier 32GB, INA3221 module rails, marginal energy = run minus same-invocation idle, 3 repeats/cell, 2026-08-13/14 catalog campaign, experiments/jetson_power/RESULTS.md); heads are transcriptions pinned byte-identical to the real backends (verify_heads.py). The measured idle floor (6.5 W mode mean) is folded into flight_power_w. Split payload sizes keep the mission-frame measurements (sweep random-input payloads recorded in hardware_grounding). Server-side and radio terms stay configured.",
